#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""RE-POOL `apixaban-vte-treatment`: read the DEFINITIONS, and watch the poolable set FALL.

THE PROPHYLAXIS HALF RAN THIS SAME DISCIPLINE AND THE POOLABLE SET WENT 3 -> 8. HERE IT GOES
8 -> 3, AND THAT IS THE SAME METHOD PRODUCING THE OPPOSITE ANSWER.

The withholding question -- does each trial report a recurrent-VTE outcome at ANY registered
rank -- was asked and recorded in `apixaban_treatment_estimand.json`. It found NINE trials with
such an outcome, EIGHT of them with posted results, including three whose registered PRIMARY is
a bleeding endpoint. That is a count of trials reporting SOMETHING NAMED recurrent VTE.

This script asks the next question, which the name cannot answer: WHAT DOES EACH ONE COUNT?

    AMPLIFY posts, at every rank, only composites carrying a DEATH term. There is no
    recurrent-VTE-alone measure anywhere in its twenty-one posted outcomes.
    AMPLIFY-EXT is the same. The six others post recurrent symptomatic VTE with NO death term
    and post nothing else.

    SO THE ESTIMAND THAT EIGHT TRIALS APPEARED TO SHARE IS SHARED BY SIX, AND THE TWO THAT DO
    NOT SHARE IT ARE THE TWO LARGEST -- 5,244 and 2,482 analysed participants.

THREE FURTHER THINGS THIS SCRIPT REFUSES, EACH FOR A STATED REASON RATHER THAN A STYLISTIC ONE.

(1) DERIVING THE MISSING ESTIMAND FROM ITS COMPONENTS. AMPLIFY posts nonfatal DVT (22/2608 vs
    35/2633), nonfatal PE (27/2606 vs 25/2632) and VTE-related death (12/2608 vs 16/2630)
    separately. Their sums are 61 and 76 against a POSTED COMPOSITE OF 59 AND 71. A derived
    estimand would have manufactured 2 and 5 events the trial's own adjudication does not
    record. The refusal is arithmetic, and it is checkable in this file.

(2) CANVAS, ON "WHAT EXACTLY WAS RANDOMISED?". Its randomised arm is a CLASS: "There are four
    FDA-approved DOAC drugs that may be used for this study: Rivaroxaban, Apixaban, Edoxaban,
    or Dabigatran", against LMWH with or without warfarin. Apixaban APPEARS in the intervention
    list and is not what was randomised, so its posted 6.1% vs 8.8% is a DOAC-class effect.
    OUR OWN MECHANICAL SCREEN PASSED IT ON THE INTERVENTION LIMB. That screen asked where the
    drug appears. This one asks what was randomised, and they disagree on a real trial.

(3) POOLING ACROSS THE COMPARATOR. AMPLIFY and AMPLIFY-EXT DO share an estimand with each other
    -- recurrent VTE or VTE-related death, primary in one and secondary in the other. They are
    still not pooled, because one randomises apixaban against enoxaparin/warfarin and the other
    against PLACEBO. That pool is computed below and declined, and it is the sharpest thing in
    this file: ESTIMAND COHERENCE IS NECESSARY AND IT IS NOT SUFFICIENT.

AND A DUPLICATE THE TEXT MATCH CANNOT SETTLE BY ITSELF -- P35 ONE LEVEL DOWN. AMPLIFY-EXT posts
its primary composite TWICE, under the same registered name, typed PRIMARY both times,
differing only in the trailing words "Randomized Population With Imputation" / "Without
Imputation" -- and the values differ by more than half again:

    With imputation      32 / 34 / 96   apixaban 2.5 mg, 5 mg, placebo
    Without imputation   19 / 14 / 77

P35 says match the registered text and never the position. When the text matches MORE THAN ONE
posted measure, choosing among the matches by position is the same defect one level down. The
choice here is an ANALYSIS-POPULATION choice, it is made once and applied to every trial, and
it is stated: the WITH-IMPUTATION analysis, because the trial's own description marks the other
as the one where "no imputation was done". Both are carried in this file and the pool is
recomputed under each.

USAGE:  python scripts/repool_apixaban_treatment_2026_08_19.py
        python scripts/repool_apixaban_treatment_2026_08_19.py --selftest
"""
